{"abstract":"As large language models (LLMs) are increasingly deployed in user-facing applications, building trust and maintaining safety by accurately quantifying a model’s confidence in its prediction becomes even more important. However, finding effective ways to calibrate LLMs—especially when the only interface to the models is their generated text—remains a challenge. We propose APRICOT (Auxiliary prediction of confidence targets): A method to set confidence targets and train an additional model that predicts an LLM’s confidence based on its textual input and output alone. This approach has several advantages: It is conceptually simple, does not require access to the target model beyond its output, does not interfere with the language generation, and has a multitude of potential usages, for instance by verbalizing the predicted confidence or using it to re-prompting the LLM to accurately reflecting its uncertainty. We show how our approach performs competitively in terms of calibration error for white-box and black-box LLMs on closed-book question-answering to detect incorrect LLM answers.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","Gubri, Martin","Lee, Hwaran","Yun, Sangdoo","Oh, Seong Joon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759425"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","South Korea"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eberhard Karls University of Tübingen","Naver AI Lab","Parameter Lab","Tübingen AI Center"],"keyword":["Uncertainty quantification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"calibrating large language models using their generations only","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2403.05973","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759425","identifier":[{"id":"85204485803","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e7e0c7a9-8533-4b00-9866-34baf318db46"],"keyword":["Confidence estimation","Language model calibration","Prompting and re-prompting","Text-based evaluation","Uncertainty quantification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-9C1919FE63C03718B309B6E4CC06775A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2403.05973","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.acl-long.824.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"parameter lab","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Parameter Lab","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"kr","key":"naver ai lab","loc":["South Korea","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Naver AI Lab","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"eberhard karls university of tübingen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eberhard Karls University of Tübingen","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"tübingen ai center","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Tübingen AI Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Thomas","key":"ulmerpau","last":"Ulmer","locid":"6596de1d-ea29-4252-a22e-f98cf28090c6","name":"Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":