{"abstract":"The field of Deep Learning (DL) has undergone explosive growth during the last decade, with a substantial impact on Natural Language Processing (NLP) as well. Yet, compared to more established disciplines, a lack of common experimental standards remains an open challenge to the field at large. Starting from fundamental scientific principles, we distill ongoing discussions on experimental standards in NLP into a single, widely-applicable methodology. Following these best practices is crucial to strengthen experimental evidence, improve reproducibility and support scientific progress. These standards are further collected in a public repository to help them transparently adapt to future needs.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","Bassignana, Elisa","Müller-Eberstein, Max","Varab, Daniel","Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob","Hardmeier, Christian","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383838"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deep learning","Experimental Standards","Natural Language Processing","Reproducibility","Scientific Methodology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental standards for deep learning in natural language processing research","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2204.06251","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383838","ids":["itu-b05d6e08-61c7-49ec-ad5d-e9ce8f0f531e"],"keyword":["Deep Learning","Experimental Standards","Natural Language Processing","Reproducibility","Scientific Methodology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8A925BE1E8372D218EFE41B5A65860A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/359937039_Experimental_Standards_for_Deep_Learning_Research_A_Natural_Language_Processing_Perspective","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2204.06251","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2204.06251.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2022.findings-emnlp.196.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Thomas","key":"ulmerpau","last":"Ulmer","locid":"6596de1d-ea29-4252-a22e-f98cf28090c6","name":"Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Max","key":"müllerebersteinpau","last":"Müller-Eberstein","locid":"523ffd96-f3b2-49cc-8f24-dc9215b84bed","name":"Müller-Eberstein, Max","orcid":"0000-0002-0006-0658","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"varabpau","last":"Varab","name":"Varab, Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2204.06251","status":"p","title":"Findings of 2022 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b05d6e08-61c7-49ec-ad5d-e9ce8f0f531e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Experimental Standards for Deep Learning in Natural Language Processing Research","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383838","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A lot of Machine Learning (ML) and Deep Learning (DL) research is of an empirical nature. Nevertheless, statistical significance testing (SST) is still not widely used. This endangers true progress, as seeming improvements over a baseline might be statistical flukes, leading follow-up research astray while wasting human and computational resources. Here, we provide an easy-to-use package containing different significance tests and utility functions specifically tailored towards research needs and usability.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","Hardmeier, Christian","Frellsen, Jes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382283"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computational Resources","Deep learning","Empirical Research","Machine learning","Statistical Significance Testing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep significance easy and meaningful statistical significance testing in the age of neural networks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87038550/2204.06815.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382283","ids":["itu-448a8623-ec53-4e7a-bb63-74fd4d673b03"],"keyword":["Computational Resources","Deep Learning","Empirical Research","Machine Learning","Statistical Significance Testing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-50089EF7987B566D5D09C90151A3C5E0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87038550/2204.06815.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Thomas","key":"ulmerpau","last":"Ulmer","locid":"6596de1d-ea29-4252-a22e-f98cf28090c6","name":"Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jes","key":"frellsenpau","last":"Frellsen","name":"Frellsen, Jes","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-448a8623-ec53-4e7a-bb63-74fd4d673b03"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"deep-significance - Easy and Meaningful Statistical Significance Testing in the Age of Neural Networks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382283","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We investigate the problem of determining the predictive confidence (or, conversely, uncertainty) of a neural classifier through the lens of low-resource languages. By training models on sub-sampled datasets in three different languages, we assess the quality of estimates from a wide array of approaches and their dependence on the amount of available data. We find that while approaches based on pre-trained models and ensembles achieve the best results overall, the quality of uncertainty estimates can surprisingly suffer with more data. We also perform a qualitative analysis of uncertainties on sequences, discovering that a model's total uncertainty seems to be influenced to a large degree by its data uncertainty, not model uncertainty. All model implementations are open-sourced in a software package.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","Frellsen, Jes","Hardmeier, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384254"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data uncertainty","Ensembles","Low resource languages","Model uncertainty","Neural classifier","Open source software","Pre trained models","Predictive confidence","Sequence analysis","Uncertainty Estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring predictive uncertainty and calibration in nlp a study on the impact of method amp data scarcity","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2022.findings-emnlp.198","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384254","identifier":[{"id":"85149889081","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cc5a86d5-a1f6-45be-bd29-0c4319271ed7"],"keyword":["Data uncertainty","Ensembles","Low-resource languages","Model uncertainty","Neural classifier","Open-source software","Pre-trained models","Predictive confidence","Sequence analysis","Uncertainty estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-325478251B4B763F29C1DED399E201FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2022.findings-emnlp.198.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2022.findings-emnlp.198","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Thomas","key":"ulmerpau","last":"Ulmer","locid":"6596de1d-ea29-4252-a22e-f98cf28090c6","name":"Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jes","key":"frellsenpau","last":"Frellsen","name":"Frellsen, Jes","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2022.findings-emnlp.198","status":"p","title":"Findings of 2022 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cc5a86d5-a1f6-45be-bd29-0c4319271ed7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring Predictive Uncertainty and Calibration in NLP: A Study on the Impact of Method &amp; Data Scarcity","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384254","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The field of Deep Learning (DL) has undergone explosive growth during the last decade, with a substantial impact on Natural Language Processing (NLP) as well. Yet, as with other fields employing DL techniques, there has been a lack of common experimental standards compared to more established disciplines. Starting from fundamental scientific principles, we distill ongoing discussions on experimental standards in DL into a single, widely-applicable methodology. Following these best practices is crucial to strengthening experimental evidence, improve reproducibility and enable scientific progress. These standards are further collected in a public repository to help them transparently adapt to future needs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","Bassignana, Elisa","Müller-Eberstein, Max","Varab, Daniel","Zhang, Mike","Hardmeier, Christian","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384979"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deep learning","Experimental Standards","Natural Language Processing","Reproducibility","Scientific Methodology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental standards for deep learning research a natural language processing perspective","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87038600/2204.06251.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384979","ids":["itu-fc23a8ce-731e-4697-aad6-c6f8388c5a44"],"keyword":["Deep Learning","Experimental Standards","Natural Language Processing","Reproducibility","Scientific Methodology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6AB440FD4ABC40E82D47ECE926F352D0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87038600/2204.06251.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Thomas","key":"ulmerpau","last":"Ulmer","locid":"6596de1d-ea29-4252-a22e-f98cf28090c6","name":"Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Max","key":"müllerebersteinpau","last":"Müller-Eberstein","locid":"523ffd96-f3b2-49cc-8f24-dc9215b84bed","name":"Müller-Eberstein, Max","orcid":"0000-0002-0006-0658","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"varabpau","last":"Varab","name":"Varab, Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fc23a8ce-731e-4697-aad6-c6f8388c5a44"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Experimental Standards for Deep Learning Research: A Natural Language Processing Perspective","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384979","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A crucial requirement for reliable deployment of deep learning models for safety-critical applications is the ability to identify out-of-distribution (OOD) data points, samples which differ from the training data and on which a model might underper-form. Previous work has attempted to tackle this problem using uncertainty estimation techniques. However, there is empirical evidence that a large family of these techniques do not detect OOD reliably in classification tasks. This paper gives a theoretical explanation for said experimental findings and illustrates it on synthetic data. We prove that such techniques are not able to reliably identify OOD samples in a classification setting, since their level of confidence is generalized to unseen areas of the feature space. This result stems from the interplay between the representation of ReLU networks as piece-wise affine transformations, the saturating nature of activation functions like softmax, and the most widely-used uncertainty metrics.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","Cinà, Giovanni"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383954"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pacmed BV"],"keyword":["Deep learning","Out of distribution detection","ReLU Networks","Safety critical Applications","Uncertainty Estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"know your limits uncertainty estimation with relu classifiers fails at reliable ood detection","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.05329.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383954","identifier":[{"id":"85122412587","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b80af5a9-b1ae-45c4-b002-93bdd1b99f5b"],"keyword":["Deep Learning","Out-of-Distribution Detection","ReLU Networks","Safety-critical Applications","Uncertainty Estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3AFD65C7D25B3743EAB374AA0AE524C0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.05329.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"pacmed bv","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Pacmed BV","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Thomas","key":"ulmerpau","last":"Ulmer","locid":"6596de1d-ea29-4252-a22e-f98cf28090c6","name":"Ulmer, Dennis Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Giovanni","key":"cinàpau","last":"Cinà","name":"Cinà, Giovanni","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["26403498"],"journal":"Proceedings of Machine Learning Research","pages":"1766-1776","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of Machine Learning Research","volume":"161"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163330329"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b80af5a9-b1ae-45c4-b002-93bdd1b99f5b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Know Your Limits: Uncertainty Estimation with ReLU Classifiers Fails at Reliable OOD Detection","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383954","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Data for multiple common susceptibility alleles for breast cancer may be combined to identify women at different levels of breast cancer risk. Such stratification could guide preventive and screening strategies. However, empirical evidence for genetic risk stratification is lacking. METHODS: We investigated the value of using 77 breast cancer-associated single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) for risk stratification, in a study of 33 673 breast cancer cases and 33 381 control women of European origin. We tested all possible pair-wise multiplicative interactions and constructed a 77-SNP polygenic risk score (PRS) for breast cancer overall and by estrogen receptor (ER) status. Absolute risks of breast cancer by PRS were derived from relative risk estimates and UK incidence and mortality rates. RESULTS: There was no strong evidence for departure from a multiplicative model for any SNP pair. Women in the highest 1% of the PRS had a three-fold increased risk of developing breast cancer compared with women in the middle quintile (odds ratio [OR] = 3.36, 95% confidence interval [CI] = 2.95 to 3.83). The ORs for ER-positive and ER-negative disease were 3.73 (95% CI = 3.24 to 4.30) and 2.80 (95% CI = 2.26 to 3.46), respectively. Lifetime risk of breast cancer for women in the lowest and highest quintiles of the PRS were 5.2% and 16.6% for a woman without family history, and 8.6% and 24.4% for a woman with a first-degree family history of breast cancer. CONCLUSIONS: The PRS stratifies breast cancer risk in women both with and without a family history of breast cancer. The observed level of risk discrimination could inform targeted screening and prevention strategies. Further discrimination may be achievable through combining the PRS with lifestyle/environmental factors, although these were not considered in this report.","author_count":212,"contributors":["Mavaddat, Nasim","Pharoah, Paul D P","Michailidou, Kyriaki","Tyrer, Jonathan","Brook, Mark N","Bo